</text></expected><extra><text /></extra><display><text>HIDE</text></display></testcase></testcases></question><question type="coderunner"><name><text>Q4 — K-fold cross-validation splits</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;div style="background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:5px solid #c9a227;border-radius:8px;padding:18px 22px;margin-bottom:16px;"&gt;&lt;p style="color:#92400e;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 9px 0;"&gt;Q4 &amp;mdash; CROSS-VALIDATION&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="color:#1e293b;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;margin:0;"&gt;Section 1.6 stressed that the training error is a biased estimate of the risk, and that K-fold cross-validation is the standard remedy.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p style="font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:15px;color:#1e293b;line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 12px 0;"&gt;Write &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;k_fold_indices(n, k)&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; returning a list of k tuples &lt;code&gt;(train_idx, test_idx)&lt;/code&gt;. Use the deterministic &lt;em&gt;strided&lt;/em&gt; assignment: fold &lt;em&gt;f&lt;/em&gt; receives the indices &lt;code&gt;f, f+k, f+2k, ...&lt;/code&gt;. Within each tuple both index lists must be sorted in increasing order.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div style="background:#fdf4ff;border:1px solid #e9d5ff;border-left:5px solid #9333ea;border-radius:8px;padding:14px 20px;margin:14px 0;"&gt;&lt;pre style="color:#3b0764;font-family:'Courier New',monospace;font-size:13.5px;margin:0;background:none;border:none;line-height:1.6;"&gt;k_fold_indices(6, 3)[0]  -&amp;gt;  ([1, 2, 4, 5], [0, 3])&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="background:#f0f9fa;border:1px solid #b9dde1;border-left:5px solid #026573;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 18px;margin:14px 0;"&gt;&lt;p style="color:#0f3f45;font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;margin:0;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hint.&lt;/strong&gt; Build the folds first, then for each fold concatenate the others and sort.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>2.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.0000000</penalty><hidden>0</hidden><idnumber /><coderunnertype>python3</coderunnertype><prototypetype>0</prototypetype><allornothing>0</allornothing><penaltyregime>0</penaltyregime><precheck>0</precheck><hidecheck>0</hidecheck><showsource>0</showsource><answerboxlines>20</answerboxlines><answerboxcolumns>100</answerboxcolumns><answerpreload>def k_fold_indices(n, k):
